  <title id="ctdivergeconverge-title">Two diverge-converge phases in sequence</title>
  <desc id="ctdivergeconverge-desc">Two diamond shapes side by side. In each, the left half widens from a point and holds many idea dots: this is divergent thinking, where options are generated and judgment is deferred. The right half narrows to a point and holds only a few dots: this is convergent thinking, where options are evaluated and selected. The first diamond is about understanding and defining the problem, the second about generating and selecting solutions. An arrow from the end of the second diamond returns to the start of the first, because testing a solution often exposes a new problem.</desc>
